19s less connected (only connects to T5 or T7-T8, you have T7 but no T8). T4 is part of T2-T3-T4 which is nearly a Chow, but you only have one each, so it\u2019s not a guaranteed meld yet.  \n\nConsidering opponents\u2019 discards:  \n- Next player melded T9 Pung and B7-B8-B9 Chow, so they may need B or T suits.  \n- Across player has B and T melds, so T tiles may be dangerous.  \n- Previous player has W1-W2-W3 Chow, so W tiles may be safer for you to keep.  \n\nThus, discard a T tile that is less likely to give others a Chow or Pung. T6 is relatively safe because T6 hasn\u2019t been heavily played (only 1 T6 in history across all players? not shown discarded much), and T7 is in your hand reducing others\u2019 Chow chances.  \n\nReason: I choose T6 because it\u2019s an isolated middle tile with high unseen count, less risky for feeding opponents\u2019 melds, and helps move toward Half Flush by removing non-W/non-honor tiles. Keeping T2-T3-T4 gives future Chow potential if you draw T1 or T5, and keeping T7 gives T6-T7-T8 potential if you draw T8.  \n\nAnswer: Play T6"}
